when you Save a game [nh3] you typically answer "y"es to the first question:
"Really save?" and then "n"o to the second question about explore-mode. this
doesn't feel quite right and seems to be inviting a costly accident where the
hacker types two "y"'s inadvertently. changing the first question to:
"Continue playing?" to get a typical "n"o response is better but still not
quite right since a double "y"es should be the proper sequence. a better
solution would have three alternatives to the "Really save?" question: [yno?]
where "y" saves the game, "n" continues to play, "o" allows you to set the
optional explore-mode with a [yn] question and "?" explains your choices.

